@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

@*Test Connection for AB#3*@


@*Header, includes Culver's logo in a Banner colored by Culver's blue*@
<div class="bannerStyle">
    <div class="headertxt">
        <h1 class="display-4">
            Why Culver's should come to Stillwater
        </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="logo">
        <img src="~/photos/culvers logo.jpg" alt="Culver's logo" />
    </div>
</div>


<div class="pageSize">
    

    @*Picture of Physical Culver's Store*@


    @*Brochure style Advertisement, three columns each blue with white borders*@
    <div class="columnsContainer">
        @*1st Column explaining Whats Culver's Is*@
        <div class="colStructure">
            <p class="cPara">
                Culver's is a Fast Food Chain founded in 1984 based in Wisconsin. 
                It's one of the fastest growing chains in the United States 
                and provides higher quality food than almost every other fast food restaurant available
            </p>
            @*Butterburger with a Concrete Shake*@
            <img src="~/photos/culvers-bb-w-concrete.jpg" class="picRes" alt="Culver's Butterburger with Concrete Style Shake and Cheese Curds" />
        
        </div>

        @*2nd Column Highlighting key menu items*@
        <div class="colStructure">
            <p class="cPara">
                Culver's Menu-Culver's is mainly Burgers and Shakes, with it's main burger being the Butterburger.
                Because Culver's is based in the Midwest, it sells some typical Wisconsin/Midwest foods such as Cheese curds, Pretzel bites
            </p>
            @*Culver's Menu*@
            <img src="~/photos/culvers menu.jpg" class="picRes" alt="A variety of Items from Culver's Menu" />

        </div>


        



    </div>
    <br />

    <div class="bulletBox">
        <p class="cPara">
            Culver's is one of the fastest growing burger chains in the United States,
            adding a net 56 stores. For comparison, Shake Shack trailed them
            with a net 50 store openings.

            However, there is not a Culver's in the state of Oklahoma.
            All states bordering Oklahoma have a combined 65 stores,
            and Stillwater should be one of the first locations in the state to get one.
        </p>

        <img src="~/photos/culvers locations.jpg"
             class="map" alt="Culver's Locations by State" />
    </div>
    
  


    <br />



    <h1 class="bluetxt">The Reasoning </h1>
    <ul class="bluetxt, bold">
        <li>
            Stillwater has a population of about 50,000,and is a college campus with thousands of students
            who reguarly go out for fastfood and
            is more akin to the family target market than somewhere like OKC and Tulsa
        </li>
        <li>
            We also host many major events that attracts tens of thousands
            of people like America's Greatest Homecoming, Calf Fry, Football games and more
        </li>
        <li>
            With a Culver's in Stillwater it would be a popular regional sport for nearby families
            and also provide a quality competition to most of the more stale restaurants nearby.
        </li>
    </ul>


</div>